---
const FAQS = [
  {
    q: 'How many Carats are in 1 Ratti?',
    a: 'Under the standard certified Pakka Ratti ratio, 1 Ratti is equal to 0.9100 Carats (182 milligrams). In traditional market trade (Sunee Ratti), 1 Ratti is counted as 0.9000 Carats (180 milligrams).'
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I convert Carats to Ratti?',
    a: 'To convert Carats to Ratti, divide the Carat weight by 0.91 (or multiply by 1.0989). For example, a 5.00 Carat gemstone is equal to 5.49 Pakka Ratti.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Why do astrologers recommend "Sawa" (e.g., Sawa 5, Sawa 7 Ratti)?',
    a: 'In Vedic Jyotish numerology, the fraction +0.25 (Sapada / Sawa) signifies growth, expansion, and positive momentum. Astrologers universally recommend Sawa weights (such as 5.25 or 7.25 Ratti) for wearing planetary gemstones to amplify beneficial results.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Why should "Paune" (+0.75) weights be avoided?',
    a: 'Paune (Padona / -0.25 from the next whole number, such as 4.75 or 6.75) denotes deficit or incompleteness in orthodox Vedic astrology. Astrologers traditionally advise against wearing Paune gemstone weights.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How is gemstone weight calculated from body weight?',
    a: 'The classical Vedic guideline prescribes 1 Ratti of gemstone weight for every 10 to 12 kilograms of human body weight. For instance, an individual weighing 65 kg requires between 5.42 and 6.50 Ratti, making Sawa Chhah (6.25 Ratti) the ideal auspicious target.'
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between Pakka Ratti and Sunee Ratti?',
    a: 'Pakka Ratti (0.91 Carats / 182 mg) is the scientifically certified standard recognized by gemological testing laboratories across India. Sunee Ratti (0.90 Carats / 180 mg) is a traditional rounded trade estimate.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How many Cents or Points are in a Carat?',
    a: '1 Carat is divided into exactly 100 Cents (also known as points). Therefore, 1 Pakka Ratti (0.91 Carats) equals 91 Cents.'
  }
];
---

<section id="faq-section" class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-8">
  <div class="rounded-3xl atelier-card p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold font-mono text-amber-700 uppercase tracking-wider" data-i18n="faqTitle">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 font-display" data-i18n="faqSubtitle">
        Everything You Need to Know About Ratti & Carat
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3 divide-y divide-slate-100">
      {FAQS.map((faq) => (
        <details class="group pt-3 first:pt-0">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none py-2 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-amber-700 transition-colors">
            <span>{faq.q}</span>
            <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-slate-100 group-open:bg-amber-100 text-slate-600 group-open:text-amber-800 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-mono transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">
              ↓
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed pt-2 pb-3">
            {faq.a}
          </p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
